sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cavia porcellus Holocene (0 Ma) Turing wavelength at 126.7 µm (tier-5 detail s0) — MorphoEval overall 80.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 scores the dispersion law, the spiral render, the epsilon and substrate sweeps, the ablation, and the specimen scale-bar segmentation. It does not credit the charge sweep or the seed ensemble; those are remediation for the v2 audit. Analytical lambda_c = 126.7 µm, numerical eigenvalue Pearson r = 1 (roundoff RMSE = 0), simulated radial peak 128.55 µm, gallery-field wavelength 78.18 µm. Overall 80.8/100 (faithfulness 79.6, reproducibility 83.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit cc4b7fb74d981b19349d4808476e5b8b2b12f75a; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 78, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at cc4b7fb74d981b19349d4808476e5b8b2b12f75a, image/png, 567960 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 ecf63291fef200a169b447a1c3de119b4e6815f66763bcfc57eb0a1fd59f9f9d (sha256 ecf63291fef200a169b447a1c3de119b4e6815f66763bcfc57eb0a1fd59f9f9d), spec_fingerprint 6023b337ad820eb039944062d27303cbeeca1ff69b22a1423b528112c7a5bbc6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6023b337ad820eb039944062d27303cbeeca1ff69b22a1423b528112c7a5bbc6; artifact_sha256: ecf63291fef200a169b447a1c3de119b4e6815f66763bcfc57eb0a1fd59f9f9d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=6cf1e5c9b49da4a2..., datasets/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=42014eaf5b445ec5...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion: a homogeneous steady state stable to k = 0 can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses farther than the activator. | Murray (1981) identified that selected wavelength with mammalian coat stripes and spots. Schnakenberg (1979) supplied the activator-substrate kinetics used here. | Swift & Hohenberg (1977) and Cross & Hohenberg (1993) give the real amplitude equation whose linear spectrum peaks at a prescribed k_c. | Sick et al. (2006) showed a WNT/DKK reaction-diffusion interaction sets mammalian hair-follicle spacing, the anatomical neighbour of a ~100 µm pigment wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian at a = 0.08, b = 1.15, gamma = 1, with D_v/D_u = 40 scaled so lambda_c = 126.7 µm exactly (D_u = 169.175 µm^2, D_v = 6767.013 µm^2). | Swift-Hohenberg spiral of charge 2 on a periodic 1.0136 mm window (eight critical wavelengths), plus an epsilon sweep, a below-onset decay, and a plain-diffusion ablation.; transfer_boundary: 126.7 µm is the slot-assigned tier-5 detail length (0.0001267 m, log10 = -3.897) for extant Cavia porcellus at 0 Ma, not a measurement quoted from a guinea-pig histology paper. | The Cavia chronoseries has one node. The 1267 µm and 12.67 µm neighbours are adjacent size tiers at the same age, not other chronospecies.; does_not_claim: That the gallery pigment field is a published micrograph, or that its measured dominant wavelength (78.18 µm on the printed 100 µm bar) equals 126.7 µm. | A full nonlinear two-species Schnakenberg integration. The rendered field is the Swift-Hohenberg amplitude equation. | Machine execution of the Lean file: this image has no lean binary.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.5]: Label the Pearson/RMSE pair as an eigensolver identity.",
            "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=2.5]: Score the charge sweep and the seed-ensemble CV, including the bin-width caveat.",
            "remediation needed: Credit the topological-charge sweep (m = 1, 2, 3) only after reporting that all three charges fall in the same radial bin k = 0.9856 (lambda = 128.55 µm).",
            "remediation needed: Report the four-seed wavenumber ensemble. At this bin width the CV is 0 because every seed shares that bin; do not describe it as a sub-bin robustness proof.",
            "remediation needed: State in the morphometric rationale that Pearson r = 1 and RMSE = 0 are the eigensolver identity of the quadratic formula, not an independent integrator residual." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.808"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (xAI), primary assessor. No second-company assessor was run in this cloud session." ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

